Summary of changes:

**`consteval.py` (new file)**: Contains deduplicated consteval operations:
- `_transpose_weight()` — CPU-side weight transpose (replaces 4 identical `cpu_hoisted_const_eval_*` functions)
- `_transpose_concat_qkv()` — CPU-side QKV transpose+concat (replaces `cpu_hoisted_const_eval_a07936ce`)
- `_to_device_bf8b()` — transpose + tile + cast to BFLOAT8_B on device (replaces 65 identical functions)
- `_to_device_bf4b()` — transpose + tile + cast to BFLOAT4_B on device (replaces 64 identical functions)
- `_concat_qkv_to_device_bf8b()` — QKV concat + tile + cast to BFLOAT8_B (replaces 31 functions)
- `_concat_qkv_reorder_to_device_bf8b()` — same but with slice+reorder for layer 31 (replaces 1 function)
- `_reshape_inv_freq()` — reshape rotary embedding frequencies (replaces 1 function)
- `run_consteval(weights, device)` — single entry point that transforms all weights in a loop over 32 layers, plus embed_tokens, lm_head, rotary_emb, and 3 constant tensors. Uses descriptive new keys like `"model.layers.N.self_attn.qkv_proj.parametrizations.weight.original"`, `"attention.neg_inf_scalar"`, `"attention.position_ids"`, `"attention.zero_scalar"`.

**`model_ttnn.py`**: 
- Removed all 166 `main_const_eval_*` functions, 5 `cpu_hoisted_const_eval_*` functions, and `consteval__main` (~28k lines eliminated)
- `__init__` now calls `consteval.run_consteval(self.weights, device)` 
- Forward function references updated from `ce_cache__main["main_const_eval_N"]` to proper `weights["..."]` keys
- Removed `ttir_cpu` import, added `consteval` import

